V4 BLOCK ACCEPTED; D2 EXACT REVIEW TARGET V5 is now frozen.

The independent reviewer found that v4 board prose exceeded the frozen bytes: mapping family/directed roles and explicit epoch/discontinuity seams were not yet bound into canonical relation identity/coalescing or exercised by separate courts; two edition playback PTS phrases also survived. That is a real contract failure. V4 is superseded.

Current main: 0b414b443e62cf4ee67a7f81e4846c2a8c13ab36.
Plan SHA-256: e132aa3a74a19fe411068c4d45f2d9d9a6fc55e7b1a78d6a41bfbe197753f223 (747 lines).
Notes SHA-256: 4949b0852e1d09fbeaf6f673e05bc51e98bcfab9373fd06a6798ffcf44d89677 (5447 lines).
git diff --check: clean. Two-file scope: 208 insertions, 21 deletions.

Focused v5 repairs now present in bytes:
- relation identity binds mapping family, directed source/target axis roles, exact geometry, occurrences, explicit epoch/discontinuity seams, and endpoints;
- canonical coalescing additionally requires same family/direction and no gap, hold, epoch, or discontinuity seam;
- holding axes/segments fixed while swapping family/direction must change identity or refuse;
- deleting an explicit seam before equal-coefficient coalescing must change identity/support or refuse;
- plan text, court, cumulative notes, and decision register carry those clauses;
- edition playback PTS no longer occurs; the audience-facing ontology is edition playback axis;
- prior v4 repairs remain: independent PTS/DTS missingness, packet-duration unknown, exact rational versus typed quantization/refusal, and historical §120.6 preserved with evolution in §121.

Documentation-only pre-C1 contract; no runtime or acquisition authority. Review these exact bytes only. I will not mutate them without another hash and supersession.
